{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTowerLift","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTowerLift","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.cable_width_wall","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.cable_width_wall","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L186-L203","doc":"**WALL (scope-(a)) — the derived cable width / brane-tower level does not close\nthe A=3 residual `0`-fit.**  At the derived (color) width `w = 3` (level `H₉`) the\nmagnitude is strictly positive (sign derived, `#4360`) but `≠ μ₃` (near-miss,\n`0.63× μ₃`); and any level that *does* close needs a strictly larger derived\n`h⁴`-coefficient (ratio `μ₃/0.297 > 1`), which no substrate rule supplies — the\none candidate (`n★ = ℓ·n₀ + k`) is refuted, overshooting.  Right sign, right order,\nexact closure open — not a fit, not a hard structural exclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.closing_needs_larger_coefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.closing_needs_larger_coefficient","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L166-L182","doc":"**Closing forces a strictly larger coefficient than the derived width's.**\nIf the derived width gives magnitude `0.297` at coefficient `κ₉` and a level with\ncoefficient `κ★` closes (`= μ₃`), then `κ★ / κ₉ = μ₃ / 0.297 > 1` (the shared\n`E₀·h⁴` cancels).  So any closing level has a **strictly larger** `h⁴`-coefficient\nthan the derived (color) level — its width is not the derived width.  This\n*quantifies* the missing `~1.585×` coefficient without inverting `μ₃` to set it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.closing_coefficient_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.closing_coefficient_exists","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L154-L164","doc":"**A closing coefficient always exists mathematically** — for `E₀ ≠ 0`, `h ≠ 0`\ntake `κ★ = μ₃/(E₀·h⁴)`.  This is the crux of the WALL: closure is a *coefficient\nexistence*, so the physics question is not \"does some `κ` close?\" (it always does)\nbut \"is the closing `κ` **substrate-derived**?\" — and the derived (color) width's\ncoefficient gives `0.297`, not `μ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.derived_width_not_closes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.derived_width_not_closes","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L146-L152","doc":"**The derived width does NOT close the A=3 residual.**  Its magnitude is\n`0.297 ≠ 0.4708 = μ₃`.  (Stated with the derived value as an explicit hypothesis\nso `μ₃` never sets the coefficient.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.derived_width_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.derived_width_positive","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L141-L144","doc":"**Right sign at the derived width** (`#4360`): the derived-width magnitude is\nstrictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.derivedWidthMagnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.derivedWidthMagnitude","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L135-L137","doc":"The derived (color width `3` ⇒ `H₉`) magnitude — the `0`-fit probe value from\n`#4364`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.μ₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.μ₃","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L132-L133","doc":"The A=3 residual target moment (`AdditiveResidualSimplex #4320`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.levelMagnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.levelMagnitude","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L127-L130","doc":"Level magnitude `c₃^L = E₀ · h⁴ · κ_L`, the coefficient model formalized in\n`BorromeanMagnitudeLift` (`levelMagnitude`).  `κ_L` is the level's `h⁴`-coefficient\n(count of Brunnian `h⁴` strand-pair configurations), set by the strand count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.level_A3_eq_nine_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.level_A3_eq_nine_iff","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L116-L123","doc":"**What the width buys, stated as an equivalence (PROVED).**  The A=3 level is\n`H₉` **exactly when** the per-nucleon width is `3`.  Unlike\n`level_is_H9_of_rule` this is falsifiable in both directions and needs no class\nat all: it is the honest form of \"the level is derived from the width\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.level_is_H9_of_rule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.level_is_H9_of_rule","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L103-L114","doc":"**From the derived width rule, the A=3 level is forced to be `H₉`** — the\nlevel is *derived* from the width input, not chosen.\n\nThe parenthetical that used to sit here — *\"Non-vacuous conditional: the level is\ncomputed from the class field, not assumed\"* — was the part to disbelieve, and it\nis deleted.  The level *is* computed from the width, but `is_color` makes the\nwidth `3` in every model, so `H₉` was never at risk and this said no more than\n`derived_level_A3` above.  What the width actually buys is the `iff` below; this\nstatement is its forward half at the colour width. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.not_widthRule_width_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.not_widthRule_width_four","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L96-L101","doc":"**A concrete non-model (PROVED).**  A width-4 cable is not the colour width,\nso the hypothesis is not satisfied by every width function.  This is the family\nthe header's `lift_is_coefficient_ratio` argument rules out: a wider cable is a\nlarger `κ`, never a different `h`-order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.not_widthRule_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.not_widthRule_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L91-L94","doc":"**…and it fails at any width differing from `3` anywhere (PROVED).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.colorRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.colorRule","kind":"instance","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L85-L89","doc":"**The rule is satisfiable, at the derived colour width (PROVED).**  So\n`[SubstrateWidthRule w]` for an *unspecified* `w` asserts only that some width\nsatisfies it; a downstream result must say which `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.SubstrateWidthRule.is_color","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.SubstrateWidthRule.is_color","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The width is the colour count `3` for every nucleon count `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.SubstrateWidthRule.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.SubstrateWidthRule.mk","kind":"ctor","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L81-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.SubstrateWidthRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.SubstrateWidthRule","kind":"class","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L62-L83","doc":"**Substrate width rule, as a predicate ON a given width function.**\n\n`w` is a per-nucleon-count cable width; `SubstrateWidthRule w` asserts that this\nparticular `w` is the `SU(3)_color` rule.\n\n**Restated 2026-08-24 (bean `qou-2y13`).**  `w` was a *field* of the class and\n`is_color` its only proposition, so the class pinned its own datum to a constant:\n`SubstrateWidthRule` had exactly one model (up to `funext`), the global instance\n`colorRule` supplied it, and `[SubstrateWidthRule]` was `w = fun _ => 3` spelled\nas a hypothesis — a binder that constrained nothing.  Taking the width as a\n*parameter* (the remedy worked in `QOU/Archimedean/JetOrderIndependence.lean`)\nmakes the hypothesis falsifiable: it holds of the colour width\n(`colorRule`) and fails of any other (`not_widthRule_of_ne`, and concretely\n`not_widthRule_width_four`).\n\nNote what this does **not** touch: whether `cableWidthColor = 3` is derived from\nthe SU(3) colour content rather than fitted.  Take that at face value — it is a\nclaim about the physics, argued in the header, and the defect here was purely\nstructural. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.derived_level_A3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.derived_level_A3","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L59-L60","doc":"The A=3 derived level is `H₉`: three nucleons × derived color width `3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.cableWidthColor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.cableWidthColor","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L53-L57","doc":"**The derived cable width of a nucleon is `3`** — the `SU(3)_color` /\nthree-quark strand count, i.e. the canonical `n₀ = 3A` atomic-braid rule (three\nstrands per nucleon).  This is *derived* from the color content of a confined\nparticle, **not** chosen to hit any target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.jointTraceStrands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.CableWidthBraneTower.jointTraceStrands","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/CableWidthBraneTowerLift.lean#L48-L51","doc":"The `A`-nucleon joint trace lives at level `H_n` with `n = A · w`, where `w`\nis the per-nucleon cable width (strand count).  `#4364` used `A = 3`, `w = 3`\n⇒ `H₉`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}